# COUPLING PROBE #2 — does the lemma dependency RECUR on a second design?
#
# The FIFO probe established one measured coupling: a data-integrity property
# that is true but not inductive, closed by a pointer+count+memory lemma. One
# design is one observation. This asks the same question of mv_filter, whose
# lemma would be a single SCALAR (the sample counter) — a different shape, so a
# positive answer is about the dependency PHENOMENON rather than one invariant.
#
#   mvf_tap        CONNECTIVITY CONTROL. Read it FIRST. counter_q can never
#                  exceed THRESHOLD, so this passes iff the tap is really wired;
#                  an undriven 4-bit wire takes 11..15 and fails. Two runs of
#                  the FIFO probe were silently meaningless for exactly this
#                  reason, so it is checked before anything else is believed.
#   mvf_equiv      the dependent property alone: q_o agrees with the model.
#   mvf_state      the lemma ALONE (no -DCLASS_MVF_EQUIV). A lemma task that
#                  also asserts the property it supports can never pass while
#                  that property is unprovable — circular, and it made the FIFO
#                  probe fail at a line that had nothing to do with the lemma.
#   mvf_equiv_lemma  the property with the lemma ASSUMED. Sound only if
#                  mvf_state passes; until then this proves nothing.
#   mvf_equiv_mut  NEGATIVE CONTROL, must FAIL. The model must detect a broken
#                  filter. It reads only the DUT's INPUTS, never q_o, so it
#                  cannot inherit the mutation — the defect that made the FIFO's
#                  negative control silently vacuous.
#
# NO `expect` lines: an expectation would prejudge what is being measured.
#
# Reading it:
#   mvf_state PASS + mvf_equiv_lemma PASS + mvf_equiv UNKNOWN + mut FAIL
#       -> the dependency RECURS on a second, held-out design. Experiment 13
#          can then be re-run across two families and stops being deterministic.
#   mvf_equiv PASSES alone
#       -> no coupling here; the property is inductive by itself and this design
#          simply does not exhibit the phenomenon. That is a real answer too.
#   mvf_equiv_mut PASSES
#       -> the model checks nothing. Ignore every other task in this file.
#
# depth 24, matching mvf.sby: the flag needs THRESHOLD=10 qualifying samples
# plus reset before it can rise, so a shallower base case cannot reach the
# behaviour the negative control depends on.

[options]
mode prove
depth 24

[engines]
smtbmc z3

[script]
verilog_defines -DCLASS_MVF_TAP
read_verilog mvf.v
read_verilog -sv mvf_fv.v
prep -top mvf_fv

[files]
gen/mvf.v
gen/mvf_mut.v
mvf_fv.v
